# Private / internal — not part of the public repository
/CLAUDE.md
/docs/project-sources/

# docs/development stays private by default. Only the explicit public guides
# below are exceptions; other working notes and Project Sources remain private.
#
# The trailing /* matters. A pattern of `/docs/development/` excludes the
# directory itself, and Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a
# later negation could never re-include anything inside it. Excluding the
# *contents* leaves the directory visible and makes the explicit negations effective.
/docs/development/*
!/docs/development/macos-setup.md
!/docs/development/first-flash.md
!/docs/development/ota-physical-validation.md
!/docs/development/architecture.md
!/docs/development/ui-rendering.md

